  "question": {
    "text": "The number of real numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math> for which the equality&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, holds for all real <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> which are not integral multiple of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></math> is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Infinite",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We have, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></math></p><p>It is possible, when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></math> has only two solution.</p>"
  }
